 { An extra pawn often doesn't suffice for victory when there are opposite-coloured bishops, but here Black has been forced to misplace his bishop to save the b6-pawn. Carlsen proceeded with subtlety. } 1. { -KEY- } Bc4 $1 { Looking for zugzwang. } ( { In contrast, the tempting } 1. b4 $6 cxb4 2. Bb3 Ke7 3. Kc6 Kf6 4. Kd6 Kg7 5. Ke7 { fails to } b5 $1 6. axb5 Bb6 { - Baburin, when the bishop manages to capture the pawns on g3 and f4 before sacrificing itself for the b-pawn, with a theoretical draw. } ) 
Ke7 $2 ( { The active } 1... Kg7 $1 { heading for h6 would have been a better option, as noticed by ex_IM. In this way, Black neutralizes the h4-h5 break which will play a key role in the game, while also creating the potential threat of ...Kh5-g4. For instance, } 2. Kc6 Kh6 3. Be2 Kg7 4. Kd5 { (4.h5 or 4.g4 doesn't yield much either, since after further pawn trades, just one passed pawn emerges on the kingside, which is easily blocked by Black's king) } Be1 5. Bf3 Kh6 $1 { , waiting for White's king to move towards the e-file before taking on g3. } ) 
2. Kc6 Kf6 3. Bd3 $1 { Zugzwang - any black move now has a clear defect. } Kf7 ( { If } 3... Ke6 { then } 4. g4 $1 fxg4 ( { or } 4... Kf6 5. gxf5 gxf5 6. h5 { etc } ) 
5. Bxg6 Kf6 ( { after } 5... g3 6. Be4 Kf6 7. h5 Kg7 8. f5 Kg8 9. Bd5 Kg7 10. Kb7 { Black is in zugzwang } ) 
6. Be4 Kg7 7. Kb5 $1 { (zugzwang) } Kh6 8. f5 g3 9. Kc6 Kh5 10. Bf3 $1 Kh6 11. Kb5 Kh7 12. h5 Kg7 13. Bd5 $1 { with a final, decisive zugzwang - Baburin. With the text move 3...Kf7 Black avoids such a breakthrough, but allows a different one. } ) 
4. h5 $1 gxh5 5. Bxf5 Kf6 6. Be4 { At this point, the black bishop must have been dreaming of changing places with the c5-pawn. } Kg7 7. Bf3 Kh6 8. Kb5 Kg6 9. Bd1 $1 ( { Seeing that } 9. Bc6 $6 { permits } Kf5 { intending ...h5-h4, Carlsen loses a tempo in order to reach the same position with Black to move. } ) 
Kh6 10. Be2 Kg6 11. Bf3 Kh6 12. Bc6 $1 ( { After } 12. Bc6 Kg6 13. Be8 Kh6 14. Bf7 { the fate of the h5-pawn is sealed, so Black resigned. } ) 

